2026-08-24T20:36:50Z	tried	what=a false disk alarm caused by the rotation itself	config=samples now carry their writing node; the disk trend compares within one box only, and needs a 30-minute window before it will extrapolate	produced=the alarm cleared; 119 tests pass; selftest still fires all 10 alarms	claim=MEASURED	control=two suppression tests (a rotation, a bootstrap) plus a test requiring a genuine one-box slope AND the free-space cliff to still fire — suppressions without that third test would be indistinguishable from switching the alarm off	why=The alarm was right that free space had dropped by 850 GB and wrong that anything was filling: it compared two different machines. Worth recording because the general shape bites any long-haul metric — most of them are about the RUN and survive a box change, and the few that are about the MACHINE do not. A false critical on a routine event is how an alarm gets ignored, so it earned a fix and not a threshold.	node=42504
